-- Regression pins for the deontic breach-semantics fix cluster:
--
--   (b) RAND/ROR over ANY both-breached pair (DeadlineMissed and/or
--       ExplicitBreach) reports a breach instead of a residual. A breach is
--       dated at the event that revealed it. RAND reports the earlier and ROR
--       the later when separate events reveal them; one event revealing both
--       is a tie, and a tie, like any pair with an ExplicitBreach, goes to the
--       left for RAND and the right for ROR, whichever deadline came first.
--   (c) the event whose timestamp reveals deadline expiry is re-offered to
--       the HENCE/LEST continuation instead of being silently consumed, and
--       the continuation's clock starts at the missed deadline.
--   (d) the deadline boundary is strict: arriving exactly AT the deadline is
--       timely; a violated prohibition reuses the event stamp as its
--       "deadline" sentinel.
--   (e) EXACTLY in per-argument position.
--   (f) a revealing event is handed on, layer by layer, to the first layer
--       whose window it is not past. A rule that names itself with a window
--       never open is refused: ok/deontic-stalled-chain.l4.
--   MAY expiry routes to LEST (default FULFILLED) per the table in
--   doc/reference/regulative/consequences.md; HENCE fires only on exercise. The HENCE
--   and LEST continuations here differ in party AND action so the golden
--   output distinguishes which branch fired.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
  pay HAS amount IS A NUMBER
  deliver
  smoke
  exercise

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (b) both alternatives breached
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`ror both explicit` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed first")
    ROR
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "missed second")

-- Both alternatives definitively breached => single breach (not a residual OR).
-- ExplicitBreach is untimestamped, so ROR reports the RIGHT operand.
#TRACE `ror both explicit` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`rand both explicit` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed first")
    RAND
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "missed second")

-- RAND over an untimestamped pair reports the LEFT operand ("the reason").
#TRACE `rand both explicit` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`explicit or deadline` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed payment")
    ROR
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`deadline or explicit` MEANS
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)
    ROR
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed payment")

-- Mixed breach kinds, both operand orders: a single breach, the right operand.
#TRACE `explicit or deadline` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

#TRACE `deadline or explicit` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`one breached one pending` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed payment")
    ROR
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

-- Separate events: RAND reports the earlier breach and ROR the later,
-- whichever side each is on. One event: a tie, left for RAND and right for ROR,
-- whichever deadline came first.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`short then long and` MEANS (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5) RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`long then short and` MEANS (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10) RAND (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`short then long or` MEANS (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5) ROR (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`long then short or` MEANS (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10) ROR (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5)

-- RAND, separate events: Alice, at 7, from either side.
#TRACE `short then long and` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 7
    WAITUNTIL 20

#TRACE `long then short and` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 7
    WAITUNTIL 20

-- ROR, separate events: Bob, at 20, from either side.
#TRACE `short then long or` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 7
    WAITUNTIL 20

#TRACE `long then short or` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 7
    WAITUNTIL 20

-- RAND, one event: the left side, Alice then Bob.
#TRACE `short then long and` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

#TRACE `long then short and` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

-- ROR, one event: the right side, Bob then Alice.
#TRACE `short then long or` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

#TRACE `long then short or` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`explicit and deadline` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed payment")
    RAND
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`deadline and explicit` MEANS
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)
    RAND
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed payment")

-- Mixed breach kinds under RAND, both operand orders: the left operand.
#TRACE `explicit and deadline` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

#TRACE `deadline and explicit` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

-- Control: only ONE alternative breached, the other still live => residual
-- (Bob may still deliver); the compound must NOT breach yet.
#TRACE `one breached one pending` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 7

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (c) the deadline-revealing event is re-offered to the continuation
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`late delivery discharges the reparation` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 100
  WITHIN 5
  LEST (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

-- Bob's delivery AT 7 both reveals Alice's expiry (7 > 5) AND is the very
-- action the LEST reparation waits for => FULFILLED (not a pending residual).
#TRACE `late delivery discharges the reparation` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 7

`prohibition hence sees the revealer` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  SHANT smoke
  WITHIN 5
  HENCE (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

-- Same re-offer on the prohibition HENCE path: the prohibition was respected,
-- and the revealing delivery discharges the HENCE obligation => FULFILLED.
#TRACE `prohibition hence sees the revealer` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 7

-- A kept prohibition is discharged at the end of its window, so its HENCE counts
-- from 5 and is due at 15: on time at 15, late at 16.
#TRACE `prohibition hence sees the revealer` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 15

#TRACE `prohibition hence sees the revealer` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 16

`anchor at the deadline` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 1
  WITHIN 2
  LEST (PARTY Alice MUST pay 2 WITHIN 3)

-- The continuation's clock starts at the missed deadline, 2, so it is due at 5.
-- Bob at 4 leaves 1 of its 3; Bob at 7 reveals that it was missed too.
#TRACE `anchor at the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 4

#TRACE `anchor at the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 7

`nested peel` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 1
  WITHIN 2
  LEST (PARTY Alice MUST pay 2 WITHIN 3 LEST (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10))

-- The layers are due at 2, 5 and 15. WAITUNTIL 20 is past all three, so it is
-- handed on down the chain and reveals the breach of layer 3: dated at 20, with
-- its deadline at 15. Bob's delivery at 35 is not reached.
#TRACE `nested peel` AT 0 WITH
  WAITUNTIL 20
  WAITUNTIL 30
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 35

-- A late payment inside the grace period discharges it. A later one does not,
-- whatever was recorded first: the 14 days run from the missed day 30, so they
-- close at 44, and the same payment gets the same verdict on all three traces.
`payment with late fee` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 1000
  WITHIN 30
  HENCE FULFILLED
  LEST
    PARTY Alice
    MUST pay 1100
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `payment with late fee` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1100 AT 40

#TRACE `payment with late fee` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1100 AT 5000

#TRACE `payment with late fee` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 31
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1100 AT 5000

#TRACE `payment with late fee` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 4999
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1100 AT 5000

-- Revealed late, but the reparation is still open at the reveal: on time.
#TRACE `payment with late fee` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 31
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1100 AT 44

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`one event repairs both alternatives` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 2 LEST (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10))
    ROR
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 2 WITHIN 3 LEST (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10))

-- Re-offer x ROR interaction: the single late delivery reveals expiry on BOTH
-- alternatives and is then re-offered inside each, fulfilling both LESTs.
#TRACE `one event repairs both alternatives` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 5

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (d) at-deadline boundary; SHANT stamp-as-deadline sentinel
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`pay due` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 100
  WITHIN 5

-- Exactly AT the deadline: timely.
#TRACE `pay due` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 100 AT 5

-- Clock advanced exactly TO the deadline: not yet expired (residual WITHIN 0).
#TRACE `pay due` AT 0 WITH
  WAITUNTIL 5

-- Strictly past the deadline: breach, "deadline, which was at 5".
#TRACE `pay due` AT 0 WITH
  WAITUNTIL 6

`no smoking` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  SHANT smoke
  WITHIN 30

-- Prohibited action exactly AT the deadline is still a violation; the breach
-- record reuses the event stamp as its "deadline" sentinel (both fields 30).
#TRACE `no smoking` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES smoke AT 30

-- Prohibition respected once the deadline has passed => FULFILLED.
#TRACE `no smoking` AT 0 WITH
  WAITUNTIL 31

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (e) EXACTLY in per-argument position
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`pay exactly 100` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay EXACTLY 100
  WITHIN 30

#TRACE `pay exactly 100` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 100 AT 10

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- MAY expiry routes to LEST; HENCE fires only on exercise
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- HENCE (Bob delivers) and LEST (Alice pays 50) are deliberately
-- DISTINGUISHABLE — different party and action — so these traces pin the
-- ROUTING, not just the outcome: were expiry mis-routed to HENCE, the first
-- trace would leave Bob's delivery obligation as a residual instead of
-- FULFILLED.
`may with lest` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MAY exercise
  WITHIN 5
  HENCE (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)
  LEST (PARTY Alice MUST pay 50 WITHIN 20)

-- Permission NOT exercised: expiry routes to LEST (Alice's reparation
-- payment), and the revealing payment is re-offered to it => FULFILLED.
#TRACE `may with lest` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 50 AT 7

-- The LEST counts from the missed 5, so it is due at 25.
#TRACE `may with lest` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 50 AT 26

-- Permission exercised: the HENCE obligation (Bob delivers) becomes the
-- residual.
#TRACE `may with lest` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES exercise AT 3

`may bare` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MAY exercise
  WITHIN 5

-- Bare MAY expiry: LEST defaults to FULFILLED (same outcome as before).
#TRACE `may bare` AT 0 WITH
  WAITUNTIL 9

`may or else breach` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MAY exercise
  WITHIN 5
  LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "permission not used"

-- A LEST BREACH after a MAY breaches when the permission goes unused, and only
-- then.
#TRACE `may or else breach` AT 0 WITH
  WAITUNTIL 9

#TRACE `may or else breach` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES exercise AT 3

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (f) an event is handed on to the first layer whose window it is not past
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`three layers` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 1
  WITHIN 2
  LEST (PARTY Alice MUST pay 2 WITHIN 3 LEST (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 100))

-- The delivery at 7 is past layers 1 and 2, due at 2 and 5, and inside layer 3,
-- due at 105, so it performs layer 3. A later event changes nothing.
#TRACE `three layers` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES deliver AT 7

#TRACE `three layers` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES deliver AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 200

-- Past layer 3 too: a breach at 106 of the deadline at 105.
#TRACE `three layers` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES deliver AT 106

-- A middle layer with no window of its own is passed through like any other.
`zero in the middle` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 1
  WITHIN 5
  LEST (PARTY Alice MUST pay 2 WITHIN 0 LEST (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 10))

#TRACE `zero in the middle` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES deliver AT 12

-- Three no-smoking windows, 0-5, 5-10 and 10-15. Smoking at 12 is inside the
-- third, whatever was recorded first: the act is not lost on the way to it.
`three prohibitions` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  SHANT smoke
  WITHIN 5
  HENCE (PARTY Alice SHANT smoke WITHIN 5 HENCE (PARTY Alice SHANT smoke WITHIN 5))

#TRACE `three prohibitions` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES smoke AT 12
  WAITUNTIL 20

#TRACE `three prohibitions` AT 0 WITH
  WAITUNTIL 11
  PARTY Alice DOES smoke AT 12
  WAITUNTIL 20

-- A WITHIN that computes below zero: the rule was past its deadline when it was
-- entered, so it fails then, at 0, and not before it existed. The cure counts
-- from 0 and is due at 3, so a delivery at 1 performs it, and it is not a breach
-- of a cure that closed at -7.
GIVEN `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`cure after a negative window` `days` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 1
  WITHIN `days` - 30
  LEST (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 3)

#TRACE `cure after a negative window` 20 AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 1

#TRACE `cure after a negative window` 20 AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 4

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- `l4 batch` prints this whole file and parses it again for each line of input,
-- so this file also pins the printing of #TRACE with several events, and of a
-- rule under a HENCE or LEST (the CLI suite runs it through batch).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export default a trivial entrypoint, so that batch has a function to call
`always true` MEANS TRUE
